    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n80415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλᾰς</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>near, hard by</i>, c. gen. ,
			which commonly stands before 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. , Τηλεμάχου π. ἵστατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.257
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νείλου π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				308
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1038
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1671
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ τάδ᾽ ἀγχόνης π</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				246
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>HF</u>
				1109
			</span></i> ; also before its case, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῆς Κασταλίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.39
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				138
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὕτη π. σοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1474
				</span></i>
			 ; separated from its case, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				580
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. dat.,
